    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“ <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span>! Did I say you could run off? Do you want to be in more trouble, young man?”</span> You turn to see a woman dressed in pretty professional attire, looking like she just came out of an office meeting. She has the same color hair as  <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span>, though much more organized and well-kept, tied up into a ball. The glasses on her face sat in front of her glaring eyes, which seem to intimidate  <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span> enough to make him quickly apologize and jump back to her side. <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Sorry mom!”</span> He says, giving a nervous smile, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I just saw my friend and forgot. Won’t happen again!”</span>  <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span> salutes his mother like she is some military commander. She sighs at this, placing her phone into her nice leather purse before reaching out to shake your hand. She has a firm grip. <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Hi there, I’m  <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Courtney</span>,  <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span>’s mother. Pleasure to meet you.”</span> She says as  <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span> sways about next to her smiling, unable to sit still for a minute. This seems to mildly annoy her. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I ask that you forgive my outburst.  <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span> here is grounded and is supposed to be helping me with the errands, not running off to tackle his friends.”</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“It was just a hug.”</span>  <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span> laughs, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“But yeah, I did an oopsie. So, I’m being mom’s best assistant ever to make up for it!”</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Well, you are better than the last one I had. Even if neither of you can listen.”</span> She says under her breath, <span style="color:Pink">patting <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span> on the head who takes it like a dog being praised.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“But grounded means no talking with friends. Come on now, we have a lot of stuff to pick up-”</span>  <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span>’s Mom turns and is about to walk <span style="color:LightCoral">away when she nearly collides with your returning Father!</span> They both stumble back, apologizing to each other. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Oh, sorry about that I-”</span> They both freeze, <span style="color:Yellow">a look of recognition of each of their faces!</span> <br>
    <br>
    <<linkreplace"Continue">>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“C-  <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Courtney</span>!?”</span>  <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Your Father</span> begins to look very nervous but tries to keep on a smile, which just makes him look a little scared. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“F- f- fancy meeting you… Well, you’re looking… H… hi?”</span> <span style="color:Yellow">He stumbles out his words in a way you’ve never seen, causing you to raise an eyebrow.</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">James</span>.”</span>  <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Courtney</span>, on the other hand, <span style="color:Yellow">speaks with clarity and a bit of venom.</span> She glares at  <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Your Father</span>, crossing her arms. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I had heard you moved back, though I haven’t had the displeasure of seeing you yet.”</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Y- yeah…”</span>  <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Your Father</span> responds with somehow more awkwardness as now both you and  <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span> are watching this with a confused expression. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Oh, is this your son? He’s-”</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“We were just leaving.”</span> She grabs  <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span> by the arm and begins to drag him away.  <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span> looks a little surprised, but waves happily to you as they depart. This leaves just you and  <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Your Father</span> standing there as you turn to him with a very confused look, asking him what that was about.

