:: Jackson Parental Drama 3 [nobr]

/* Intro */
You sit down next to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span>, who is currently trying to rip apart a rather tough piece of Salisbury steak with his teeth, and ask him how he is doing. He manages to rip a piece off after a moment and happily enjoys it while giving you a thumbs up. Once he swallows, you ask him if he recalls your meeting at the mall the other day.

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
            },
        },
            {
            Name: "Jackson",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Uniform",
                Mouth: "Happy",
                },
            },
        ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Yeah, that was funny.”</span> He chuckles, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Mom was acting so weird, never seen her like that before. Well, I guess I have, but it’s rare. She was a bit grumbly afterwards though. Was weird.”</span> As he goes in for another bite, you explain that you may have figured out why both your parents were acting so weird. Turns out that your dad and his mom used to date back in high school! You don’t know the specifics, but from what you’ve gathered, it was a bit of a messy breakup.  <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span> nods along as you explain, <span style="color:Yellow">though honestly seems more interested in the slab of meat he is eating.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“That makes sense. Mom never talks about when she was a kid.”</span>  <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span> says with a full mouth, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I used to think she was always an adult! But why would breaking up something make her act so weird? Then again, if it was messy she would be mad. She hates when stuff is messy. Last time I tracked mud into the house she got so mad she grabbed this spoon and-”</span> As  <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span> explains you get the feeling he isn’t fully understanding what you mean and you try to explain. Your parents used to date when they were younger. Like hugging and kissing and stuff. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“But that’s gross! Besides, my mom only kisses my dad and me and my brother.”</span>  <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span> waves off your thoughts as if they are crazy, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Why would our parents kiss each other? That’s really weird.”</span>  <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span> goes in for his mashed potatoes <span style="color:Yellow">as you realize he isn’t going to understand what you mean.</span> <br>
<br>
You sigh, starting to eat your own food as you wonder what could have led to such a messy breakup and why they acted so weirdly around each other. The curiosity is eating you up inside, so you turn to  <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span> and ask if he’d be willing to pry and ask his mom about it, but he shakes his head. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Mom doesn’t like when I ask unimportant questions. Says she gets a lot of that at work, and it hurts her head.”</span>  <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span> pauses, swallowing the food in his mouth. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“My dad might know though. He knows EVERYTHING and loves answering questions. If you ever come over, you can ask him about it.”</span> <br>
<br>
You nod, accepting this as the best you are going to get. For now, you’ll drop the topic. But maybe in the future you can try to ask  <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span>’s dad about it. <span style="color:Yellow">You hope it wasn’t anything too bad that would affect your friendship with <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span>.</span> <br>
